{
  "note": "Development hub path (ticket 26/09/23 U5, coordinator rule 23): an explicitly named hub is JOIN-ONLY (a serve waits with a localized status and gives up after a declared bound, never starts a hub); only the default hub is started, behind an owner lease per port and data root; the owner republishes a catalog the current hub cannot load. `roles`: explicit hub url → role. `locales`: POSIX locale variables → terminal language. `statuses`: every status and its exact en/de line. `leases`: records the lease reader accepts (`valid`) or refuses (`invalid`), which the schema `DevHubLeaseV1` must classify the same way. `catalogs`: a data root's trusted catalog (pointer + generation header) → freshness (`absent` / `current` / `stale` with the reason's leading words). `joins`: a fake hub that binds after `bindsAfterMs` (null: never) and the join bound → outcome. `owns`: the default-hub path under a lease state and port state → whether an owner is spawned, the status kinds reported, and the outcome.",
